### Metering requests (mesure_synchrone_auto/v2). Per Enedis, the metering APIs cannot be tested in
### the sandbox (it returns placeholder dates such as 20XX-XX-XX), so these requests target PROD
### ({{ENEDIS_API_PROD}}). 99999999999999 is a placeholder: replace it with a real PRM whose holder
### has consented to your application, and set a real PROD token in http-client.private.env.json
### (ENEDIS_TOKEN).
### dateDebut is inclusive; dateFin is exclusive and cannot equal dateDebut.

### Daily consumption.
GET {{ENEDIS_API_PROD}}/mesure_synchrone_auto/v2/consommation_quotidienne
    ?pointId=99999999999999&dateDebut=2025-05-01&dateFin=2025-07-14
Authorization: Bearer {{ENEDIS_TOKEN}}

### Daily production.
GET {{ENEDIS_API_PROD}}/mesure_synchrone_auto/v2/production_quotidienne
    ?pointId=99999999999999&dateDebut=2025-05-01&dateFin=2025-07-14
Authorization: Bearer {{ENEDIS_TOKEN}}

### Consumption load curve. Limited to 7 consecutive days (dateFin exclusive, so 2025-05-01 to
### 2025-05-08 is the maximum window).
GET {{ENEDIS_API_PROD}}/mesure_synchrone_auto/v2/courbe_de_charge_consommation
    ?pointId=99999999999999&dateDebut=2025-05-01&dateFin=2025-05-08
Authorization: Bearer {{ENEDIS_TOKEN}}

### Production load curve. Same 7-day limit.
GET {{ENEDIS_API_PROD}}/mesure_synchrone_auto/v2/courbe_de_charge_production
    ?pointId=99999999999999&dateDebut=2025-05-01&dateFin=2025-05-08
Authorization: Bearer {{ENEDIS_TOKEN}}
